+# 📦 Import Management for Namespaced Poly Repo
+
+## 🎯 Overview
+
+This document describes the **3-way import management system** designed specifically for the `haive` namespaced poly repo structure. The system handles the unique challenges of absolute imports in a monorepo where packages use the `haive.*` namespace.
+
+## 🏗️ The Challenge
+
+In a namespaced poly repo like `haive`, you encounter several import-related challenges:
+
+1. **Absolute imports requirement**: All imports should use `from haive.core import X` not `from .core import X`
+2. **Bad import patterns**: Avoiding `from src.haive` or `from packages.haive`  
+3. **Missing imports**: Automatically adding correct namespace imports
+4. **Cross-package dependencies**: Handling imports between `haive-games`, `haive-dataflow`, etc.
+
+## 🚀 The 3-Way Solution
+
+### Phase 1: 🔍 Detection & Analysis
+- Scans for relative imports (`from .`, `import .`)
+- Identifies bad namespace patterns (`src.haive`, `packages.haive`)
+- Counts undefined names and unused imports
+- Provides comprehensive report before changes
+
+### Phase 2: 🧹 Bad Import Removal  
+- Converts relative imports to absolute: `from .core` → `from haive.core`
+- Fixes bad namespace patterns: `from src.haive` → `from haive`
+- Uses ruff TID251/TID252 rules to enforce absolute imports
+- Automatic sed-based pattern replacement
+
+### Phase 3: 📦 Missing Import Addition
+- Uses `autoimport` with namespace awareness
+- Custom Python logic for `haive.*` namespace detection
+- Adds missing imports based on usage patterns
+- Intelligent insertion at proper location
+
+### Phase 4: 🎯 Organization & Cleanup
+- `isort` for proper import section organization
+- `ruff` for final cleanup and unused import removal
+- Code formatting for consistency
+- Final validation and reporting
+
+## 🛠️ Tools & Configuration
+
+### Ruff Configuration (`pyproject.toml`)
+```toml
+[tool.ruff.lint]
+select = [
+    "I",           # isort
+    "F",           # Pyflakes  
+    "TID251",      # Banned relative imports (enforce absolute)
+    "TID252",      # Relative imports from parent modules
+]
+
+[tool.ruff.lint.isort]
+known-first-party = ["haive"]
+combine-as-imports = true
+force-sort-within-sections = true
+lines-after-imports = 2
+```
+
+### AutoImport Configuration
+```toml
+[tool.autoimport]
+disable_move_to_top = false
+force_absolute_imports = true
+
+[tool.autoimport.common_statements]
+# Core haive imports
+"haive.core" = "from haive import core"
+"haive.agents" = "from haive import agents"
+"haive.tools" = "from haive import tools"
+"haive.games" = "from haive import games"
+"haive.dataflow" = "from haive import dataflow"
+"haive.mcp" = "from haive import mcp"
+
+# Common Python patterns
+"Path" = "from pathlib import Path"
+"Optional" = "from typing import Optional"
+"BaseModel" = "from pydantic import BaseModel"
+```
+
+## 🎮 Usage
+
+### Quick Commands (via Taskipy)
+
+```bash
+# Preview import issues across all packages
+task preview-imports
+
+# Fix imports for specific packages
+task fix-imports-games     # haive-games only
+task fix-imports-dataflow  # haive-dataflow only  
+task fix-imports-mcp       # haive-mcp only
+task fix-imports-agents    # haive-agents only
+
+# Check current import violations
+task check-imports
+```
+
+### Manual Usage
+
+```bash
+# Preview mode (no changes)
+./dev-tools/scripts/comprehensive-import-manager.sh haive-games/src
+
+# Fix mode (apply changes)
+./dev-tools/scripts/comprehensive-import-manager.sh haive-games/src --fix
+```
+
+## 📊 Example Output
+
+```
