+
+## 🏗️ Architecture
+
+### Import Section Organization
+```python
+# 1. Standard library imports
+import os
+import sys
+from pathlib import Path
+from typing import Optional, List, Dict
+
+# 2. Third-party imports  
+import pandas as pd
+import numpy as np
+from pydantic import BaseModel, Field
+
+# 3. Haive namespace imports (absolute only)
+from haive import core, agents, tools
+from haive.core.engine import BaseEngine
+from haive.games.tic_tac_toe import TicTacToeGame
+```
+
+### Banned Patterns
+- ❌ `from .haive import X`
+- ❌ `from ..haive import X`  
+- ❌ `from src.haive import X`
+- ❌ `from packages.haive import X`
+- ✅ `from haive import X`
+- ✅ `from haive.core import X`
+
+## 🔧 Advanced Features
+
+### Custom Namespace Detection
+The system includes Python logic to detect `haive.*` usage patterns and automatically add missing imports:
+
+```python
+# Detects usage like: haive.core.BaseEngine
+# Automatically adds: from haive import core
+
+# Detects usage like: haive.games.TicTacToe  
+# Automatically adds: from haive import games
+```
+
+### Safe Operation
+- **Git stash checkpoints** before any changes
+- **Preview mode** to see what would change
+- **Incremental application** - can run on single files/directories
+- **Rollback capability** via git stash
+
+### Integration with Development Workflow
+- Integrates with existing ruff/isort configuration
+- Works with pre-commit hooks
+- Compatible with CI/CD pipelines
+- Taskipy integration for easy access
+
+## 🚨 Safety & Best Practices
+
+### Before Running
+1. **Commit or stash** any uncommitted changes
+2. **Run in preview mode** first to understand changes
+3. **Test on small directories** before applying broadly
+
+### After Running  
+1. **Review changes** with `git diff`
+2. **Test imports** by running `python -c "from haive import core"`
+3. **Run tests** to ensure nothing is broken
+4. **Commit changes** with descriptive message
+
+### Error Handling
+- Script continues on individual file errors
+- Reports warnings for tools that complete with issues  
+- Final assessment shows remaining issues that need manual review
+- Safe defaults - won't break existing working imports
+
+## 🎯 Integration Examples
+
+### CI/CD Pipeline
+```yaml
+- name: Check Import Quality
+  run: |
+    task check-imports
+    task preview-imports > import-report.txt
+    
+- name: Fix Import Issues (if auto-fix enabled)
+  run: |
+    task fix-imports-games
+    task fix-imports-dataflow  
+    git diff --exit-code || echo "Import fixes applied"
+```
+
+### Pre-commit Hook
+```yaml
+- repo: local
+  hooks:
+    - id: import-check
+      name: Import Quality Check
+      entry: ./dev-tools/scripts/comprehensive-import-manager.sh
+      args: [--preview]
+      language: system
+      types: [python]
+```
+
+This system provides comprehensive, safe, and automated import management specifically designed for the challenges of a namespaced poly repo structure. 
